{
  "id": "self-reference-effect",
  "term": "self-reference effect",
  "definition": "The self-reference effect is the tendency for information linked to oneself to be remembered or recognized better than information linked to someone else. In other words, material processed in relation to the self tends to leave a stronger memory trace.",
  "field": "cognition",
